{"cuisine/cuisine-of-liguria":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-liguria","n":"Ligurian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Italy","intro":[["Ligurian cuisine consists of dishes from the culinary tradition of Liguria, a region of northwestern Italy, which makes use of ingredients linked both to local production (such as preboggion, a mixture of wild herbs), and to imports from areas with which, over the centuries, the Ligurians have had frequent trade (such as Sardinian pecorino, one of the ingredients of pesto)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-liguria"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_Liguria"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":2,"links":[["Baxin","dish/baxin"],["Coniglio alla sanremese","dish/coniglio-alla-sanremese"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"A Small Kitchen in Genoa","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"asmallkitcheningenoa.com","note":"Genoese cook Enrica Monzani's English-language blog of Ligurian recipes.","url":"https://asmallkitcheningenoa.com/about","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Liguria: The Cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Laurel Evans","note":"Recipes from the Italian Riviera by a Liguria-based American writer, published by Rizzoli.","url":"https://rizzoliusa.com/book/9780847870615","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780847870615"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Fennel","ingredient/fennel"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Rabbit meat","ingredient/rabbit-meat"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/9/9a/Baxin.jpg","w":500,"h":330,"by":"13morris","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baxin.jpg","of":"Baxin"}},"ingredient/maida-flour":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/maida-flour","n":"Maida flour","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Maida is a type of wheat flour originated from the Indian subcontinent. It is a refined wheat flour used in Indian cuisine to make pastries and other bakery items like breads and biscuits. Some maida may have tapioca starch added."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-maida-flour"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maida_flour"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Awadhi cuisine","cuisine/awadhi-cuisine",[["Sheermal","dish/sheermal"]]],["Iranian cuisine","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",[["Sheermal","dish/sheermal"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Maida (flour)","ingredient/maida-flour"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Saffron","ingredient/saffron"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/49/Maida_flour.jpg/500px-Maida_flour.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Thamizhpparithi Maari","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maida_flour.jpg"}},"dish/ayam-panggang":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ayam-panggang","n":"Ayam panggang","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Ayam panggang is a variety of ayam bakar chicken dish from the cuisine of the Cocos (Keeling) Islands. The dish is differentiated from other Malay cuisine chicken dishes by the thick sauce that coats the chicken. The recipe was developed due to the living conditions of the Cocos (Keeling) Islands, giving rise to a dish much more dependent on coconut. The dish is made across the Cocos Malay diaspora, in Sabah, Malaysia as well as Western Australia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ayam-panggang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayam_panggang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"],["Gepuk","dish/gepuk"]]}]},"dish/calisson":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/calisson","n":"Calisson","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Calissons are a traditional French candy consisting of a smooth, pale yellow, homogeneous paste of candied fruit (especially melons and oranges) and ground almonds topped with a thin layer of royal icing. They have a texture similar to that of marzipan, but with a fruitier, distinctly melon-like flavour. They are often almond-shaped and are typically about five centimeters (two inches) in length."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-calisson"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calisson"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Almond meal","ingredient/almond-meal"],["Candied fruit","ingredient/candied-fruit"],["Fondant icing","ingredient/fondant-icing"],["Melon","ingredient/melon"],["Syrup","ingredient/syrup"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["A