of small sausage, usually containing minced pork, or sometimes minced chicken."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chipolata"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chipolata"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beer","ingredient/beer"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"],["Linguiça","ingredient/linguica"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8f/-2020-07-01_Pork_chipolata_sasages%2C_Trimingham%2C_Norfolk.JPG/500px--2020-07-01_Pork_chipolata_sasages%2C_Trimingham%2C_Norfolk.JPG","w":500,"h":617,"by":"Kolforn (Kolforn) I'd appreciate if you could mail me (Kolforn@gmail.com) if you want to…","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:-2020-07-01_Pork_chipolata_sasages%2C_Trimingham%2C_Norfolk.JPG"}},"dish/greek-salad":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/greek-salad","n":"Greek salad","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Greek cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Greek salad, choriatiki or Horiatiki is a salad in Greek cuisine generally made with pieces of tomatoes, cucumbers, onion, feta cheese, and olives (typically Kalamata olives) and dressed with salt, Greek oregano, and olive oil. Common additions include lemon juice, green bell pepper, caper berries (especially on the Cyclades islands), and mint or parsley for decoration (mainly in Northern Greece). Greek salad is often imagined as a farmer's breakfast or lunch, as its ingredients resemble those that a Greek farmer might have on hand."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-greek-salad"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_salad"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Feta","ingredient/feta"],["Kalamata olive","ingredient/kalamata-olive"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Oregano","ingredient/oregano"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Dimitra's Dishes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dimitrasdishes.com","note":"Dimitra Alfieris's video channel and blog focused on classic Greek home cooking.","url":"https://dimitrasdishes.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Greek cuisine","links":[["Avgolemono","dish/avgolemono"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bouyiourdi","dish/bouyiourdi"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Diples","dish/diples"],["Fasolada","dish/fasolada"],["Freddo cappuccino","dish/freddo-cappuccino"],["Greek restaurant","dish/greek-restaurant"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kakavia (soup)","dish/kakavia-soup"],["Kalitsounia","dish/kalitsounia"],["Karydopita","dish/karydopita"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Ladera","dish/ladera"],["Noumboulo","dish/noumboulo"],["Psarosoupa","dish/psarosoupa"],["Spanakorizo","dish/spanakorizo"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Tzatziki","dish/tzatziki"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/54/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Gr%C3%A6sk_salat.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Gr%C3%A6sk_salat.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"cyclonebill","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Gr%C3%A6sk_salat.jpg"}},"dish/mongolian-barbecue":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mongolian-barbecue","n":"Mongolian barbecue","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Taiwan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mongolian barbecue is a method of preparing stir-fried noodle dishes. Despite its name, the dish is not Mongolian, nor was it influenced by Mongolian cuisine. It was developed in Taiwan by a waishengren during the 1950s. Furthermore, it is also unrelated to actual barbecue traditions (such as American or Korean barbecue), since it is not cooked on a perforated grill above the smoke of an open flame, but rather a specialized flatiron grill. The kind of grill used to cook it is in the shape of a circle, and an upside-down wok was, in 1979, used to cook the dish in Taiwanese establishments. It has more in common with Teppanyaki."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mongolian-barbecue"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongolian_barbecue"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cooking in Chinglish","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookinginchinglish.com","note":"Taiwanese home recipes from Edwina, who grew up in Taiwan.","url":"https://cookinginchinglish.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Tiny Urban Kitchen: Taiwanese Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tinyurbankitchen.com","note":"Small set of Taiwanese recipes from Jen Che, a Taiwanese American blogger in Hong Kong.","url":"https://tinyurbankitchen.com/taiwanese-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Taiwan cuisine","links":[["Ageh (food)","dish/ageh-food"],["Alivongvong","dish/alivongvong"],["Apple bread","dish/apple-bread"],["Bah-uân","dish/bah-uan"],["Braised pork rice","dish/braised-pork-rice"],["Coffin bread","dish/coffin-bread"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Egg yolk pastry","dish/egg-yolk-pastry"],["Iron egg","dish/iron-egg"],["Kiâm-piánn","dish/kiam-piann"],["Ló͘-bah-pn̄g","dish/lo-bah-png"],["Peanut ice cream roll","dish/peanut-ice-cream-roll"],["Penglai rice","dish/penglai-rice"],["Pineapple cake","dish/pineapple-cake"],["Pineapple shrimp balls","dish/pineapple-shrimp-balls"],["Pork ball","dish/pork-ball"],["Rechao","dish/rechao"],["Shuangbaotai","dish/shuangbaotai"],["Small sausage in large sausage","dish/small-sausage-in-large-sausage"],["Taiwanese beef noodle soup","dish/taiwanese-beef-noodle-soup"],["Taiwanese fried chicken","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken"],["Taiwanese fried chicken cutlet","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken-cutlet"],["Tàⁿ-á-mī","dish/ta-a-mi"],["Tea egg","dish/tea-egg"],["Ti-hueh-kué","dish/ti-hueh-kue"],["Tshik-á-mī","dish/tshik-a-mi"],["Tube rice pudding","dish/tube-rice-pudding"],["Xiaolongbao","dish/xiaolongbao"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/79/Mongolianbbq.jpg/500px-Mongolianbbq.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Matthew Levine from San Francisco, CA, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongolianbbq.jpg"}},"dish/morkovcha":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/morkovcha","n":"Morkovcha","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Morkovcha also known as Korean-style carrots or Korean carrot salad, is a spicy marinated carrot salad. It is a dish in Koryo-saram cuisine, and is a variant of banchan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-morkovcha"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morkovcha"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Daucus","ingredient/daucus"],["Daucus carota subsp. sativus","ingredient/daucus-carota-subsp-sativus"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Sunflower oil","ingredient/sunflower-oil"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maangchi","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maangchi.com","note":"Maangchi's Korean recipe site and YouTube channel, one of the best known English sources for Korean cooking.","url":"https://www.maangchi.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Korean Bapsang","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean